    "problem_statement": "On a work queue, a high-priority task that repeatedly queues a work item and immediately cancels it in a tight loop can drive the work-queue semaphore count to a large negative value, and the work_thread only processes a single item per wake. As a result, work items queued while the queue is in this inconsistent state are not triggered, so not all queued workers run. The test must verify that after such stressing the queue remains consistent: all 100 queued count workers run exactly once (call_count == VERIFY_COUNT) and all work entries are cleared (work[i].worker == NULL).",
